# Sign-symmetry probe — 5 steps forward, then 5 steps reverse.
# Final state = initial state (anchor_3a, anchor_3b), so any per-
# traversal angular-momentum leak should either:
#   (a) cancel: h_w residual after settle ≈ h_w(single-forward) − h_w(single-reverse) ≈ 0
#   (b) accumulate: h_w residual after settle ≈ 2 × h_w(single-forward)
# Distinguishes a numerical-integration leak (sign-symmetric → cancels)
# from a systematic gait-induced leak (accumulates).
#
# The swing-arm pattern is mirrored so the reverse traversal exercises
# the same arm at the same step ordinal (b, a, b, a, b → b, a, b, a, b
# but on the way home).

START anchor_3a anchor_3b

# Forward traversal: (3a,3b) → ... → (5a,6b)
DOCK  anchor_4b
DOCK  anchor_4a
DOCK  anchor_5b
DOCK  anchor_5a
DOCK  anchor_6b

# Reverse traversal: (5a,6b) → ... → (3a,3b)
DOCK  anchor_5b
DOCK  anchor_4a
DOCK  anchor_4b
DOCK  anchor_3a
DOCK  anchor_3b
